              In plagiarism detection (PD) systems, two important problems should be considered: the problem of retrieving candidate documents that are globally similar to a document
              q
              under investigation, and the problem of side‐by‐side comparison of
              q
              and its candidates to pinpoint plagiarized fragments in detail. In this article, the authors investigate the usage of
              structural
              information of scientific publications in both problems, and the consideration of
              citation evidence
