ged, such as confusing diagnoses; providing vague, ambiguous advice; or	Wilhelm, Theresa Isabelle; Roos, Jonas; Kaczmarczyk, R.	2023		10.2196/49324		(other folder)	Undermind	OASIS Lab	2	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://www.jmir.org/2023/1/e49324/PDF	True	False		Not in an ingest folder: found because it is close to the seed and Elicit papers	NEW	0.897	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.884	NEW	0.865	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.831	NEW	0.732	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.707	0.853	OASIS Lab:YFM38KEQ
Reporting-guideline compliance	Score papers against reporting or risk-of-bias checklists	S4	Screen: 2 of 3 models or DNA-VL-STEER-2B	2 of 3	yes	2	Large language models with human-in-the-loop validation for systematic review data extraction	Systematic reviews are time-consuming endeavors. Historically speaking, knowledgeable humans have had to screen and extract data from studies before it can be analyzed. However, large language models (LLMs) hold promise to greatly accelerate this process. After a pilot study which showed great promise, we investigated the use of freely available LLMs for extracting data for systematic reviews. Using three different LLMs, we extracted 24 types of data, 9 explicitly stated variables and 15 derived categorical variables, from 112 studies that were included in a published scoping review. Overall we found that Gemini 1.5 Flash, Gemini 1.5 Pro, and Mistral Large 2 performed reasonably well, with 71.17\%, 72.14\%, and 62.43\% of data extracted being consistent with human coding, respectively. While promising, these results highlight the dire need for a human-in-the-loop (HIL) process for AI-assisted data extraction. As a result, we present a free, open-source program we developed (AIDE) to facilitate user-friendly, HIL data extraction with LLMs.	Schroeder, Noah L.; Jaldi, Chris Davis; Zhang, Shan	2025		10.48550/arxiv.2501.11840		(other folder)	Undermind	OASIS Lab	2	abstract (Zotero)	False		True	False		Not in an ingest folder: found because it is close to the seed and Elicit papers; Models split	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.925	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.873	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.88	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.833	NEW	0.777	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.728	0.861	OASIS Lab:HK2YFPSC
