### Biography

John Carlisle, 51, is a consultant anaesthetist at Torbay Hospital in Devon and a critic of dubious data in medical trials. Convinced that his specialty was being polluted by false claims from the Japanese researcher Yoshitaka Fujii, Carlisle responded to a challenge to prove this, developing a statistical method that can measure how likely it is that the baseline data in a randomised trial are true. Fujii failed the test and has since had more than 160 papers retracted, probably making him the world record holder. Since then, Carlisle himself has had a paper on the wonders of the Mediterranean diet retracted—for sloppy randomisation, not dishonesty. Trialists everywhere have …"	Group, British Medical Journal Publishing	2019	BMJ	10.1136/bmj.k5318	https://www.bmj.com/content/364/bmj.k5318	Metascience	Metascience	OASIS Lab	1	abstract (Zotero)	False		False	True		Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.664	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.63	NEW	0.751	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.718	NEW	0.558	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.501	0.662	OASIS Lab:PATU7IM4
