Education research and learning interventions (new)	Synthesize education and learning research (out of scope)	N29		3 of 3	no	0	Empowering Learners: Chatbot-Mediated 'Learning-by-Teaching'	Chatbots and online learning platforms provide synthesized information to learners. However, research shows learning is particularly effective when learners themselves teach someone. Prior work has explored an interactive instructional approach called ‘Learning-by-teaching’, but this approach traditionally relies on human counterparts, limiting it to their interest and co-located settings. To overcome these limitations, we investigated whether we can empower learners using chatbot-mediated ‘learning-by-teaching.’ We designed an agnostic, open-source chatbot replicating a virtual student, to which learners teach to learn. We conducted an experiment involving 24 students to evaluate the effectiveness of chatbot-mediated teaching compared to textbook-based problem-solving practice. Results indicate that teaching the chatbot benefits student learning than textbook-based problem-solving. This work highlights the effectiveness of chatbots, envisioning their design as virtual students to mediate ‘learning-by-teaching’.	Sabnis, Nihar; Nagashima, Tomohiro	2024	Extended Abstracts of the 2024 CHI Conference on Human Factors in Computing Systems	10.1145/3613905.3650754	https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3613905.3650754	Metascience	Metascience	OASIS Lab	1	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/3613905.3650754	False	False			NEW	0.846	Peer review reports	0.827	NEW	0.731	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.725	NEW	0.571	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.564	0.737	OASIS Lab:ZQIF7XCS
