Evidence-based policy and evaluation practice (new)	Evaluate programs and rate evidence for policy	N12		3 of 3	no	0	The influence of evidence-based program registry websites for dissemination of evidence-based interventions in behavioral healthcare	"Purpose
Evidence-based program registries (EBPRs) are web-based databases of evaluation studies that summarize the available evidence for the effectiveness of behavioral healthcare programs, including programs addressing substance misuse, mental health, child welfare, or offender rehabilitation. The study determined the extent to which visitors to selected EBPRs accomplished the objectives of their visits and how often those visits resulted in the adoption of new or improved evidence-based interventions (EBIs).
Method
A follow-up telephone survey was conducted with 216 visitors to a convenience sample of six EBPRs an average of six months after the visitors’ incident visit to the EBPR.
Results
The most frequent objective was to identify evidence-based programs/services, curricula or assessments, followed by finding resources to implement or improve the preceding and writing a grant proposal including to comply with funding requirements; 71% of such objectives were achieved across the full set of objectives. Implementation of an EBI was completely achieved for 31% of relevant objectives and some progress on EBI implementation occurred for 19% of relevant objectives.
Conclusions
This is the first study to document the usage of EBPRs as a modality to increase the utilization of EBIs in the actual practice of behavioral healthcare. The results support the continued use of web-based EBPRs for disseminating information on evidence-based interventions for behavioral healthcare."	Magura, Stephen; Lee-Easton, Miranda J.; Abu-Obaid, Ruqayyah N.; et al.	2023	Evaluation and Program Planning	10.1016/j.evalprogplan.2022.102214	https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0149718922001689	Metascience	Metascience	OASIS Lab	1	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10121732/pdf/nihms-1861951.pdf	False	False			NEW	0.744	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.731	NEW	0.757	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.729	NEW	0.501	Assess ethical matters	0.484	0.693	OASIS Lab:FPTPRPN5
