Interdisciplinary science and knowledge synthesis (new)	Study how fields and scholars synthesize knowledge	N8		3 of 3	no	0	Integrate the integrators! A call for establishing academic careers for integration experts	Integration is often considered the core challenge and the defining characteristic of inter- and trans-disciplinary (ITD) research. Given its importance, it is surprising that the current system of higher education does not provide permanent positions for integration experts; i.e., experts who lead, administer, manage, monitor, assess, accompany, and/or advise others on integration within ITD projects or programs. Based on empirical results of an ITD 2019 Conference Workshop entitled “Is there a new profession of integration experts on the rise?” held in Gothenburg, Sweden, and our own experience in leading and studying ITD integration, the present article sheds light on the overarching question, “What are integration experts?”, thus contributing to the emerging literature on integration and integration expertise. We use direct quotes from participants to substantiate workshop results and triangulate them with recent literature on ITD research as well as Science of Team Science (SciTS) and Science and Technology Studies (STS). We conclude our article by discussing possible unintended consequences of establishing academic careers for integration experts, and suggest four complementary ways to support them, while mitigating potentially negative consequences: (a) establishing an international Community of Practice (CoP) to foster peer-to-peer exchange among integration experts, create greater visibility, and develop ideas for transforming academic structures; (b) studying academic careers of integration experts to provide empirical evidence of “successful” examples and disclose different ways of establishing related academic positions; (c) funding respective positions and aligning metrics for ITD research to foster integration within ITD projects or programs; and (d) engag	Hoffmann, Sabine; Deutsch, Lisa; Klein, Julie Thompson; et al.	2022	Humanities and Social Sciences Communications	10.1057/s41599-022-01138-z	https://www.nature.com/articles/s41599-022-01138-z	Metascience	JP - Personal | Metascience / JP-Personal	OASIS Lab, personal	2	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://www.nature.com/articles/s41599-022-01138-z.pdf	True	False		Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.762	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.761	NEW	0.76	Peer review reports	0.758	NEW	0.529	Assess novelty	0.506	0.7	personal:2VCTJKIS
