incompatible use of concepts and operationalizations. We show that item, scale, and label
embeddings—representations of psychometric items, scales, and construct labels in a vector
space obtained from language models—can help tackle this problem in psychology. We analyze different data sets (e.g., International Personality Item Pool) spanning thousands of items
and hundreds of scales and constructs, to show that embeddings can be used to predict empirical relations between measures, perform automated detection of jingle–jangle fallacies, and
