Meta-analysis methods (new)	Describe and critique meta-analytic methods	N18		3 of 3	no	0	A history of meta-regression: Technical, conceptual, and practical developments between 1974 and 2018	At the beginning of the development of meta-analysis, understanding the role of moderators was given the highest priority, with meta-regression provided as a method for achieving this goal. Yet in current practice, meta-regression is not as commonly used as anticipated. This paper seeks to understand this mismatch by reviewing the history of meta-regression methods over the past 40 years. We divide this time span into four periods and examine three types of methodological developments within each period: technical, conceptual, and practical. Our focus is broad and includes development of methods in the fields of education, psychology, and medicine. We conclude the paper with a discussion of five consensus points, as well as open questions and areas of research for the future.	Tipton, Elizabeth; Pustejovsky, James E.; Ahmadi, Hedyeh	2019	Research Synthesis Methods	10.1002/jrsm.1338	https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/jrsm.1338	Metascience	JP - Personal | Metascience | Metascience / JP-Personal	OASIS Lab, personal	2	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://doi.org/10.31234/osf.io/dvb6r	True	True		Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.774	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.741	NEW	0.751	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.736	NEW	0.528	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.526	0.712	personal:2JHVRBYK
