u"	Bandrowski, Anita; Brush, Matthew H.; Grethe, Jeffrey S.; Haendel, Melissa A.; Kennedy, David N.; Hill, Sean; Hof, Patrick R.; Martone, Maryann E.; Pols, Maaike S.; Tan, Serena; Washington, Nicole L.; Zudilova-Seinstra, Elena; Vasilevsky, Nicole	2015	The Journal of comparative neurology	10.1002/cne.23913		SysRev-LLMApp pool	SysRev-LLMApp	OASIS Lab, personal	2	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/pdfdirect/10.1002/cne.23913	False	False		Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.817	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.815	NEW	0.788	Assess ethical matters	0.786	NEW	0.556	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.552	0.804	OASIS Lab:FFDYTAXS
Publishing, citations and research impact (new)	Explain or predict citation, impact and publishing practices	N5		3 of 3	yes	1	A Search Engine for Discovery of Scientific Challenges and Directions	Keeping track of scientific challenges, advances and emerging directions is a fundamental part of research. However, researchers face a flood of papers that hinders discovery of important knowledge. In biomedicine, this directly impacts human lives. To address this problem, we present a novel task of extraction and search of scientific challenges and directions, to facilitate rapid knowledge discovery. We construct and release an expert-annotated corpus of texts sampled from full-length papers, labeled with novel semantic categories that generalize across many types of challenges and directions. We focus on a large corpus of interdisciplinary work relating to the COVID-19 pandemic, ranging from biomedicine to areas such as AI and economics. We apply a model trained on our data to identify challenges and directions across the corpus and build a dedicated search engine. In experiments with 19 researchers and clinicians using our system, we outperform a popular scientific search engine in assisting knowledge discovery. Finally, we show that models trained on our resource generalize to the wider biomedical domain and to AI papers, highlighting its broad utility. We make our data, model and search engine publicly available.	Lahav, Dan; Saad Falcon, Jon; Kuehl, Bailey; et al.	2022	Proceedings of the AAAI Conference on Artificial Intelligence	10.1609/aaai.v36i11.21456	https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/AAAI/article/view/21456	(other folder)		OASIS Lab	1	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://doi.org/10.1609/aaai.v36i11.21456	True	False		Not in an ingest folder: found because it is close to the seed and Elicit papers; Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.89	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.874	NEW	0.8	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.796	NEW	