Replication and reproducibility in psychology (new)	Assess replicability and replication practice	N26		3 of 3	no	0	The Replication Database: Documenting the Replicability of Psychological Science	In psychological science, replicability—repeating a study with a new sampleachieving consistent results (Parsons et al., 2022)—is critical for affirming the validity of scientific findings. Despite its importance, replication efforts are few and far between in psychological science with many attempts failing to corroborate past findings. This scarcity, compounded by the difficulty in accessing replication data, jeopardizes the efficient allocation of research resources and impedes scientific advancement. Addressing this crucial gap, we present the Replication Database (https://metaanalyses.shinyapps.io/replicationdatabase/), a novel platform hosting 1,239 original findings paired with replication findings. The infrastructure of this database allows researchers to submit, access, and engage with replication findings. The database makes replications visible, easily findable via a graphical user interface, and tracks replication rates across various factors, such as publication year or journal. This will facilitate future efforts to evaluate the robustness of psychological research.	Röseler, Lukas; Kaiser, Leonard; Doetsch, Christopher; et al.	2024	Journal of Open Psychology Data	10.5334/jopd.101	https://openpsychologydata.metajnl.com/articles/10.5334/jopd.101	Metascience	Metascience / ESS/ReSS/IReSS	OASIS Lab	2	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://openpsychologydata.metajnl.com/articles/101/files/692e9213be318.pdf	False	False			NEW	0.772	Peer review reports	0.757	NEW	0.75	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.73	NEW	0.57	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.554	0.791	OASIS Lab:3GI23674
