Reporting guidelines, preregistration and transparency (new)	Check or promote reporting completeness and preregistration	N17		3 of 3	no	0	Methods and results of studies on reporting guideline adherence are poorly reported: a meta-research study	"Objectives
We investigated recent meta-research studies on adherence to 4 reporting guidelines to determine the proportion that provided (1) an explanation for how adherence to guideline items was rated and (2) results from all included individual studies. We examined conclusions of each meta-research study to evaluate possible repetitive and similar findings.
Study Design and Setting
Cross-sectional meta-research study. MEDLINE (Ovid) was searched on July 5, 2022 for studies that used any version of the CONSORT, PRISMA, STARD, or STROBE reporting guidelines or their extensions to evaluate reporting.
Results
Of 148 included meta-research studies published between August 2020 and June 2022, 14 (10%, 95% confidence interval [CI] 6% to 15%) provided a fully replicable explanation of how they coded the adherence ratings and 49 (33%, 95% CI 26% to 41%) completely reported individual study results. Of 90 studies that classified reporting as adequate or inadequate in the study abstract, 6 (7%, 95% CI 3% to 14%) concluded that reporting was adequate, but none of those 6 studies provided information on how items were coded or provided item-level results for included studies.
Conclusions
Almost all included meta-research studies found that reporting in health research is suboptimal. However, few of these reported enough information for verification or replication."	Santo, Tiffany Dal; Rice, Danielle B.; Amiri, Lara S. N.; et al.	2023	Journal of Clinical Epidemiology	10.1016/j.jclinepi.2023.05.017	https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0895435623001312	Metascience	Metascience	OASIS Lab	1	abstract (Zotero)	True	https://www.medrxiv.org/content/medrxiv/early/2022/12/20/2022.12.19.22283669.full.pdf	True	True			NEW	0.791	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.744	NEW	0.83	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.765	NEW	0.755	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.558	0.813	OASIS Lab:B8UXSGFR
