Scientific claim verification and text mining (new)	Extract, verify or retrieve claims from the literature with NLP	N11		3 of 3	no	0	Distributional Semantics Resources for Biomedical Text Processing	The openly available biomedical literature contains over 5 billion words in publication abstracts and full texts. Recent advances in unsupervised language processing methods have made it possible to make use of such large unannotated corpora for building statistical language models and inducing high quality vector space representations, which are, in turn, of utility in many tasks such as text classification, named entity recognition and query expansion. In this study, we introduce the first set of such language resources created from analysis of the entire available biomedical literature, including a dataset of all 1to 5-grams and their probabilities in these texts and new models of word semantics. We discuss the opportunities created by these resources and demonstrate their application. All resources introduced in this study are available under open licenses at http://bio.nlplab.org.	Pyysalo, Sampo; Ginter, Filip; Moen, Hans; Salakoski, Tapio; Ananiadou, Sophia	2013	NA			SysRev-LLMApp pool	SysRev-LLMApp	OASIS Lab, personal	2	abstract (Zotero)	False	no DOI: not checked	False	False		Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.88	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.848	NEW	0.794	Detect errors / limitations / quality issues	0.778	NEW	0.582	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.563	0.76	OASIS Lab:9TUQTNJT
