Web pages, OSF projects, essays and commentary (new)	Index web resources and informal writing (little text to embed)	N19		3 of 3	no	0	Toward augmenting the human intellect and boosting our collective IQ	phy and Award 30 3 DEDICATION This book is dedicated in deep appreciation and fond memory to Yuri Rubinsky who conceived, edited and produced this very special keepsake as a heartfelt tribute to Doug Engelbart. About this book: Boosting Our Collective IQ, a selection of readings, was originally published in a special edition of 2000 copies for attendees of the 4 International World Wide Web Conference, December 1995, of which 100 were hardbound, numbered and signed by the author, Douglas Engelbart, and by Tim Berners-Lee, the inventor of the World Wide Web. This book was the brainchild of Yuri Rubinski, co-founder of SoftQuad, who in addition to organizing Doug’s 1995 SoftQuad Web Award at the conference, wished to create a special tribute for attendees that outlined Doug’s vision for the future. So in collaboration with Doug’s business partner and daughter Christina Engelbart (working under an oath of secrecy), Yuri produced this timeless keepsake to be distributed in a surprise unveiling to Doug at the award presentation. This new release has been published by MRW Connected for the Doug Engelbart Institute to mark the 40th anniversary of Doug’s 1968 Demo. Our intent was to make this important work more widely available, while still honoring the original 2000 copies as limited edition keepsakes. This new edition is a near exact replica of the original softcover edition, in its artful style and craftsmanship, with the exception of the new cover design and title page. Credits: Cover portrait of Doug courtesy of Logitech, Inc. Cover collage combines photos from Doug’s SRI lab and 1968 Demo courtesy of SRI International, diagrams from Doug’s papers included herein, and press photo of Doug with Bill Clinton courtesy the White House. Back cover photo from the 1968 Demo court	Engelbart, Douglas C.	1995	Communications of the ACM	10.1145/208344.208352	https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/208344.208352	Metascience	Metascience	OASIS Lab	1	PDF (abstract section)	True	https://dl.acm.org/doi/pdf/10.1145/208344.208352	True	False		Published 2022 or earlier: check that it involves LLMs	NEW	0.707	Peer review reports	0.7	NEW	0.754	Check  reporting guideline compliance	0.734	NEW	0.467	Assess novelty	0.434	0.654	OASIS Lab:2UI5CVYB
